A display helper is declared void but its body tries to hand a number back. What happens when the file is compiled?
class Thermostat {
    int level = 3;
    void show() {
        System.out.print(level);
        return level;
    }
}

A discount helper promises a number but only covers one of the two possible inputs. What happens when the file is compiled?
class Discount {
    int tier(int n) {
        if (n > 100) {
            return 20;
        }
    }
}

A vending helper announces itself and also reports a doubled coin count, and the caller prints what it receives. What prints?
class Vending {
    int vend(int coins) {
        System.out.print("vend ");
        return coins * 2;
    }
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Vending v = new Vending();
        int got = v.vend(3);
        System.out.print(got);
    }
}

A toll booth prices each crossing and the driver is charged for two of them. What prints?
class Lane {
    int fee(int minutes) {
        return minutes * 3;
    }
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Lane l = new Lane();
        int a = l.fee(4);
        int b = l.fee(5);
        System.out.print(a + b);
    }
}

A fan helper declares a method that must hand back twice its blade count. Fill the blank so the printed value is 10.
class Fan {
    int blades = 5;
    int describe() {
        ___
    }
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.print(new Fan().describe());
    }
}
// prints: 10

A voucher class must let main store the outcome of redeem in an int. Which of these headers, placed on the marked line, let the class compile and run? Select all that apply.
class Voucher {
    int credit = 40;
    //FILL
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int got = new Voucher().redeem(3);
        System.out.print(got);
    }
}

A gauge helper is called twice, once without using the answer and once with. What prints?
class Gauge {
    int bump() {
        int v = 3;
        v = v + 2;
        return v;
    }
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Gauge g = new Gauge();
        g.bump();
        System.out.print(g.bump());
    }
}

A tip helper is written to hand the amount back rather than print it. Why is that the better shape?
class Tip {
    int total(int bill, int pct) {
        return bill + bill * pct / 100;
    }
}

A poster tool takes five values at once and stitches them into one string. What is the main design problem with that signature?
class Banner {
    void draw(int rows, int cols, char fill, boolean border, String label) {
        System.out.print(rows + "" + cols + fill + border + label);
    }
}

A report writer marks each row as a header or a detail with a flag argument. What is wrong with that choice?
class Report {
    void emit(String row, boolean header) {
        if (header) {
            System.out.print("H" + row);
        } else {
            System.out.print("D" + row);
        }
    }
}

A number-range helper is handed a start and an end. What prints?
class Span {
    String between(int from, int to) {
        String out = "";
        for (int k = from; k < to; k++) {
            out = out + k;
        }
        return out;
    }
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Span s = new Span();
        System.out.print(s.between(2, 5));
    }
}

A range report prints nothing at all because the two numbers arrived in the wrong order. Which replacement for the marked line prints 234?
class Span {
    String between(int from, int to) {
        String out = "";
        for (int k = from; k < to; k++) {
            out = out + k;
        }
        return out;
    }
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Span s = new Span();
        System.out.print(s.between(5, 2));//FIX
    }
}
// prints: 234

A grid helper needs a row count and a column count and nothing more. Fill the blank so the printed value is 12.
class Grid {
    int cells(int rows, int cols) {
        return rows * cols;
    }
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.print(new Grid().cells(___));
    }
}
// prints: 12

A label builder takes four values and glues them into one tag. What prints?
class Tag {
    void print(String kind, int id, boolean urgent, String owner) {
        System.out.print(kind + "-" + id + (urgent ? "*" : "") + "@" + owner);
    }
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Tag t = new Tag();
        t.print("crate", 42, true, "liv");
    }
}

A report helper takes a tenant name it never mentions, yet every caller must still supply one. What is the problem?
class Fridge {
    int door = 0;
    int report(String tenant) {
        return door;
    }
}

A range class offers a one-value header and a two-value header. Which of these calls, placed on the marked line, compile and run? Select all that apply.
class Span {
    String between(int from, int to) {
        String out = "";
        for (int k = from; k < to; k++) {
            out = out + k;
        }
        return out;
    }
    String between(int from) {
        return between(from, 0);
    }
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        //FILL
    }
}

A mixer class declares two headers that share a name and differ only in how many values they take. What does that pair represent?
class Mixer {
    void pour() {
        System.out.print("0");
    }
    void pour(int ml) {
        System.out.print(ml);
    }
}

A class offers two different names for the same addition. Which response is right?
class Tally {
    int addUp(int a, int b) {
        return a + b;
    }
    int total(int a, int b) {
        return a + b;
    }
}

A scale offers a whole-number version and a decimal version, and the caller wanted the decimal one but got 2. Which replacement for the marked line prints 2000?
class Scale {
    int weight(int grams) {
        return grams;
    }
    int weight(double kilos) {
        return (int) (kilos * 1000);
    }
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scale s = new Scale();
        System.out.print(s.weight(2));//FIX
    }
}
// prints: 2000

A mixer class offers one version taking a whole number and one taking a decimal, and the driver calls both in turn. What prints?
class Mixer {
    void blend(int ml) {
        System.out.print("int " + ml);
    }
    void blend(double ml) {
        System.out.print("double " + ml);
    }
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Mixer m = new Mixer();
        m.blend(4);
        m.blend(4.0);
    }
}

A dyer class offers a version taking a number and a version taking text. Which of these calls report 1? Select all that apply.
class Dye {
    int dye(int n) {
        return 1;
    }
    int dye(String tag) {
        return 2;
    }
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Dye d = new Dye();
        System.out.print(___);
    }
}
// prints: 1

A tag class declares two headers with the same name and the same empty parameter list but different return types. What happens?
class Tag {
    String id() {
        return "a";
    }
    int id() {
        return 1;
    }
}

A box class can already be built from a number. Fill the blank so the printed value is nkn3.
class Box {
    String label;
    static Box of(int n) {
        Box b = new Box();
        b.label = "n" + n;
        return b;
    }
    ___
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.print(Box.of("k").label + Box.of(3).label);
    }
}
// prints: nkn3

Here is one header and its body. What can a caller conclude from the header alone?
class Tile {
    public static int area(int w, int h) {
        return w * h;
    }
}

A ledger keeps its running total in a private static counter and offers a private static void add plus a private static int total. Which of these expressions report 12? Select all that apply.
class Ledger {
    private static int total = 0;
    private static void add(int amount) {
        total = total + amount;
    }
    private static int total() {
        return total;
    }
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Ledger.add(5);
        Ledger.add(7);
        System.out.print(___);
    }
}
// prints: 12

A reader declares that it may raise a fault, and its caller wraps the call. What prints?
class Port {
    int read() throws Exception {
        return 7;
    }
    int go() {
        try {
            return new Port().read();
        } catch (Exception e) {
            return 0;
        }
    }
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.print(new Port().go());
    }
}

An oven program does not compile because an instance method is named on the class. Which replacement for the marked line prints heat5?
class Oven {
    int temp = 5;
    void heat() {
        System.out.print("heat" + temp);
    }
    static int spare() {
        return 12;
    }
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Oven.heat();//FIX
    }
}
// prints: heat5

A cart accumulates a total and its add method hands back the same object so calls can be chained. What prints?
class Cart {
    int total;
    Cart add(int price) {
        total = total + price;
        return this;
    }
    int count() {
        return total / 10;
    }
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Cart c = new Cart();
        c.add(30).add(20);
        System.out.print(c.count() + ":" + c.total);
    }
}

A safe class keeps its pin private and a tester in another class is refused when it names that pin. What does the header say?
class Safe {
    private int pin = 4321;
    int check(int guess) {
        return guess == pin ? 1 : 0;
    }
}

A formatter class must print 3-sky when main runs. Fill the blank with the header that makes that call work.
class Formatter {
    ___
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        report(3, "sky");
    }
}
// prints: 3-sky
